## Summary

I delivered a production-grade native Apple SwiftUI **`ReauthDialog`** surface at parity with `web/src/components/feedback/ReauthDialog.tsx`, following the repo's canonical `AiUsageCard` multi-file pattern — **12 files** under `apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/` (committed as `b052e893a`).

**What it reproduces (full parity):** credential mode (password + optional authenticator tabs) and confirm mode (typed `CONFIRM`); mode derivation from session auth-mode; the exact `totpTabAvailable` rule; TOTP sanitisation; all `sudo.*` i18n keys (1:1, `{{token}}`→`%@`); the full coded-error ladder (`REAUTH_NOT_CONFIGURED`, `INVALID_CREDENTIAL`→password/totp variants, raw/unknown); form reset on re-present; TOTP-tab fallback; cancel-guard while submitting. Plus the P4 leaf states (loading / empty / error / stale / offline), `view.opened` telemetry (slug `ReauthDialog`), a11y labels on every interactive element, and a `.reauthDialog(model)` sheet host. It binds only through the P1/S8 state-holder seam — no HTTP in the view.

